# Planning a trip from an empty file: project, a section cycled with Ctrl+T, tasks made with the type picker, an itinerary with dates, a reorder and a copied checklist.
# The file holds only a line break, as an editor leaves a new file, so the save keeps one.
file <<END

END
keys <Enter>
type Trip to Japan:
keys <Enter> <Tab>
type Before we go
keys <C-t> <C-t> <Enter>
type Book flights
keys <Enter>
type Get a JR pass
keys <Enter>
type Exchange money
keys <Enter> <S-Tab>
type Itinerary:
keys <Esc>
see ▌ Itinerary:
keys k k k J J <Tab>
see ▌     Exchange money
keys my
see Node type:
type task
keys <Enter>
see ▌     - Exchange money
keys <Esc> G i
type Day 1 Tokyo
keys <Enter>
type Day 2 Kyoto
keys <Enter>
type Day 3 Osaka
keys <Esc> k k md
see Due date
type +14d
keys <Enter>
see in 14 days
keys j W } j <A-k>
see ▌   - Day 3 Osaka
keys gg j y G p
see ▌   Before we go
quit
saved <<END
Trip to Japan:
	Before we go @section
		- Book flights
		- Get a JR pass
		- Exchange money
Itinerary:
	- Day 1 Tokyo @due({today+14})
	- Day 3 Osaka
	- Day 2 Kyoto @due({today+2})
	Before we go @section
		- Book flights
		- Get a JR pass
		- Exchange money
END
